| P3 no stop-grad -> all decay | **Established**: Tian 2021 (no SG: vec(W)' = -H vec(W), H PSD), Halvagal 2023 (rate -(1-lambda)^2), Ponce et al. 2025 (linear case without SG/EMA always collapses); empirically SimSiam (0.1%), BYOL tau=0 (0.3%). | Only the per-direction Cauchy-Schwarz form is a re-derivation; present as consistency, cite. |
| P4 no predictor fails when c <= sigma + lambda; growth window 0 < p < c/sigma; LR/init/scale move p through the window | Partly established: window = Halvagal's lambda_m(1-lambda_m) (closed-form predictor; no predictor -> no learning); Tian: larger predictor LR ratio shrinks collapse basin, too large stops growth; empirical BYOL App. I (no-EMA needs predictor LR x2+; collapse if predictor lr <= projector lr), SimSiam (no/fixed predictor fails); Wen & Li 2022 (predictor rescues weak features). | Predictor **init scale, width, depth** as an effective gain moving p through the window, and the predicted transition location: new (gap G2). Empirical anchors: I-JEPA depth 6->12 better, width 384 > 1024. |
| P5 masking sets c_k/sigma_k; rank falls with mask ratio | **Not established** (gap G3). Tools: masked moment identities (Bisulco et al. 2025; Dong et al. NeurIPS 2025), masked-PLS BBP scaling (Gjolbye et al. 2026). Empirics: I-JEPA target scale optimum (0.15,0.2), 1 vs 4 blocks 9.0 vs 54.2; V-JEPA best ~90%; LiDAR: I-JEPA rank sensitive to mask scale. | New. Caution: with disjoint Bernoulli context/target masks the cross-covariance scales like m(1-m) (non-monotone in m) while context variance falls like (1-m); check that "rank falls monotonically with ratio" survives, and note practice (V-JEPA) finds high ratios best for accuracy, not rank. |
| P6 EMA changes rate, not linear threshold | Not stated as such. Related: Tian 2021 (slower EMA enlarges collapse basin; "curriculum"), PEIRA (EMA has the same equilibria as SG, stability open), Ponce 2025 (SG/EMA equilibria asymptotically stable). Busbridge et al. 2023 EMA scaling rule (rho -> rho^kappa) is a time-scale statement, consistent with P6. Empirics: BYOL tau sweep (tau=1: 18.8, 0.99: 72.5), DINO/data2vec. | New as a linear-stability statement; must reconcile with Tian's basin-enlargement result (EMA acting through the race). |
| P7 weight decay raises threshold; stepwise rank in lambda | **Established in form** (Tian, Wang 2021, PEIRA; contrastive: Ziyin et al. 2023; deep linear: Ziyin, Li & Meng 2022; L2 on factorised map = nuclear-norm soft threshold: Kobayashi et al. 2024). | Stepwise rank at lambda = c_k^2/(4 sigma_k) with mask-dependent c_k, sigma_k and its test in neural JEPAs. |
| LeJEPA (2511.08544, 2025-11-11) | Date qualifies. Explicit isotropic-Gaussian regulariser (SIGReg), no EMA/SG/predictor needed; makes collapse impossible by construction, no dynamics theory. | Compare only as the "explicit regulariser" alternative. |

Novelty statement the evidence supports: a unified per-direction early-time
drive-vs-decay account for JEPAs that (i) covers predictor scale/init/width/
depth, masking ratio and EMA in one criterion, (ii) predicts reachable rank
from data statistics and set-up, and (iii) is tested on neural JEPAs. The
static threshold, the necessity of stop-grad and the weight-decay threshold
must be credited to Tian 2021 / Wang et al. 2021 / PEIRA 2026 / Halvagal 2023.


